WEBVTT

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:06.060
Oops... you mean Sawaki 
didn't tell you?

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:07.500
Huh?

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.480
Sawaki...

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.740
You can't see any microbes, can you?

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.990
You can't, can you?

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.680
Moyashimon

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.250
A Shining Microbe Future

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.290
Wow, this is pretty bad...

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:50.040
So, since when haven't you seen them?

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.460
Uh...

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.580
There were none in Oikawa's 
place when I went there,

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.220
since she has antibacterial 
stuff everywhere.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.300
Listen.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:01.720
Where humans exist, there is 
never an absence of microbes.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.720
Hasegawa's Mental Image

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.220
Really?

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.210
Wait, you went to Oikawa's place?

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.230
What is a girl's room like?

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:09.960
Uh, it was just...

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.110
Sawaki.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.860
Since when haven't you see them?

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.930
Uh...

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:19.710
I could definitely see them 
during the spring festival.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.490
You're sure?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:22.740
Yeah...

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.180
Anyway, about Oikawa!

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.690
So did you do it?!

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.500
No way.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.720
You liar!

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:29.750
That's enough!

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.430
You two, get out of here! 
You're in the way!

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.170
Please tell us, Master Sawaki!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:34.800
Oh...

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.080
Since then?

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.120
Since when?

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:42.430
Uh, well...

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.300
<i>I can't say it.</i>

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.700
Hey, there's only one thing

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.180
a guy and a girl could do 
in a girl's room, right?

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.360
Nah, Sawaki doesn't have 
the guts to do that.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.270
What do you think, Hasegawa-san?

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.150
I think you should shut up!

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.030
Sawaki-kun, there you are!

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:02.410
So that gothic lolita 
girl is Yuuki-kun?!

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.410
That's just not right!

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.910
You shouldn't kiss another guy!

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.410
Uh... I agree...

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:11.720
You kissed...

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:12.420
...a guy?!

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.130
That's unclean! Unclean!

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.420
Unclean!

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.070
So what if it's between guys?

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.640
Now you're unclean, too.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.350
I don't care about that 
right now! Just be quiet!

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.970
R-Right...

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.650
Okay, putting aside when 
you lost your ability.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.470
If you can't see microbes...

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.910
you're just some shrimp.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.700
Yeah... that's true, but...

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.800
Now, now, Hasegawa-san...

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.670
That doesn't matter, does it?

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.590
It does matter!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:04.210
What if you can never 
see microbes again?

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.350
What reason will you have to be here?

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.650
Hasegawa-san, that wasn't necessary.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.350
Yeah. You're going too far.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:14.830
Sawaki is Sawaki. 
Isn't that good enough?

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.430
Even if the ability he had, 
that we don't have, is gone,

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.810
it's not like we lose anything.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:21.830
He's not just some shrimp.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.360
Let's get something to eat, Sawaki.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.770
I'm hungry.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.600
So there you go. We're going 
out to eat with Sawaki.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.700
Lend us some money.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.870
Take Oikawa and get out of here.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.400
Don't let it get to you.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.510
Yeah.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:50.610
Hey!

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.150
Hasegawa lent us money!

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:57.500
Hey, how long are you going to be 
knocked out from Hasegawa's kiss?

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.400
Let's buy some meat with 
this and have a hotpot!

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.770
Why hotpot? It's hot as hell out.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.470
Whatever, let's just 
go get something good.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.080
What do you want, Sawaki?

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.740
Anything's fine.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:17.040
Damn it, why do I...

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.730
Don't be in a hurry.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:27.740
Things can't always go 
the way you planned.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:30.810
Not for yourself, or for others.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.520
Did you decide what you want to eat?

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.360
We've got plenty of funds.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.860
Sorry. I'm just going 
to go home for today.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.860
Get Oikawa something to eat.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:47.940
Thanks a lot.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:20.100
Excuse me... is Kei here?

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:21.610
Kei?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.480
Yes.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.110
Sorry, there's no one 
here with that name...

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.240
Sawaki...

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:42.750
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.630
I see... so you lost the ability again.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.690
That hasn't happened since summer 
of our second year in high school.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:40.770
Yeah.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:42.750
But it happens pretty often, right?

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:46.760
Yes. But Hasegawa-san 
doesn't know that.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:51.040
She was asking what I'd do if 
I could never see them again.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.760
How am I supposed to answer that?

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:57.020
What do you want to happen, Sawaki?

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.560
Would it be easier on you 
if you couldn't see them?

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:02.910
You've had some hard times

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:05.770
since you were little 
because of that ability.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:11.020
But maybe it's better 
if I can see them.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:14.180
I mean, Professor Itsuki 
expects a lot of me.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:19.540
What should I do? I don't know.

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:21.540
Yeah...

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.050
I think it's up to you.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:33.880
Up to me?

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:34.840
Yeah.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:37.880
It's hard to live so that 
everyone will like you,

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:41.060
but if people find out that that's 
your goal, they won't like you.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.310
Is that how I look to other people?

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.540
I see.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:50.640
Sorry.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.320
It's okay.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:58.700
Anyway, why did you take 
leave from school?

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:01.960
And why did you decide to do that?

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:03.880
Does it look bad on me?

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.280
That's not what I meant.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.760
Don't you think that, 
before they're born,

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.370
everyone has the potential 
to become anything,

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:15.370
even the president of 
the USA or the Pope?

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:17.140
Y-Yeah...

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:20.610
And out of all the things I could be,

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.780
I chose to be the only 
son of Yuuki Liquors.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.450
Life is made of choices,

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:28.770
and making choices means 
abandoning other possibilities.

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:33.280
I thought that seemed sort of wasteful.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.770
I still don't get it.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.410
Get what?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.910
You always got mad when anyone 
said you looked girly.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:44.660
So why would you want 
to dress like that?

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:46.960
I guess I never would have

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:50.420
thought of wearing this before now.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:53.760
But I think a person's 
mentality lies underneath

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.330
the things they insist that they hate.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:59.430
You always take things to extremes.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:01.600
I decided before I came here

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.190
that I'd try lots of things before 
going back to the country.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:07.530
I see.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:11.480
I really wasn't thinking of anything.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:15.200
What did I come to college to do?

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:21.200
What's all this?

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.830
Did he figure out who you were?

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:30.430
Well, as long as you're alive, 
you can come up with new secrets.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:32.140
What do you say, boy?

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:35.490
Still loving those 
microbes like always?

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:54.360
So, whose story should I listen to first?

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:57.380
Aya-san, listen to me!

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:01.310
No, let's talk about my 
plans after graduation.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:02.490
Bombay on the rocks.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:03.670
Forget that!

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.810
Aya-san, we want your opinion.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:06.660
Yeah.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:10.110
Well then, talk fast!

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:12.250
What was it? Something 
about an ability...

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:15.360
The question was, if you had an 
ability that no one else had,

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:19.260
and then you suddenly lost 
it, what would you do?

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:22.300
You just keep drinking, Mutou-san.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.410
What do you think, Aya-san?

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:27.520
If you suddenly lost a 
unique ability one day...

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.020
Well...

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:32.150
If that was all you had going 
for you, you'd be finished.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:34.270
There wouldn't be anything 
appealing about you anymore.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.530
We weren't asking you, little girl!

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.370
You're meaner than you 
look, Hazuki-chan.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:43.290
I am? Then what do you think?

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:46.240
I like guys who are losers.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:50.210
So I guess I'd look for other 
good things about him.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:53.000
I might find something 
else to like in him.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.210
You're so mature!

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:58.550
That's right. Humans 
aren't that shallow.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.850
Yeah. Hasegawa's just childish.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:03.630
Who are you guys talking about, anyway?

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:05.020
Hey, look, there's an ant here.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:05.390
Oh, there is.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:09.970
That's right... Oikawa doesn't 
know about Sawaki's ability.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:10.890
Yeah.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:15.020
Hey, what do you think I should do?

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:18.200
Stay in college, or get a job?

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:20.240
Here's your Bombay.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.400
That's it!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.330
But do you think Sawaki's okay?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.660
I wonder...

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:29.830
Come here, microbes!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.580
Write "Sawaki" like you did before!

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.640
Write "Sawaki"!

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:39.920
Come on, yeasts!

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.260
To carry on the Sawaki business that

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:50.400
has been running since the Muromachi era.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:52.890
That's my duty.

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:53.990
No!

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:58.190
It just fell onto me because 
my brother went and got a job.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.410
A fun, extravagant campus life in Tokyo.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:10.580
That's all I was thinking of.

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:24.290
What am I doing?

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.640
I'm acting like a kid.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:51.960
Damn...

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.690
I forgot to shut off the alarm.

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:58.900
What should I do today?

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.720
Sawaki

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.360
I see.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.600
You guys were always there.

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:22.860
It sure is quiet this morning.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:25.190
I hope what I said will give

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:27.740
Sawaki-kun a little more motivation.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.370
Will he even come here again at all?

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:35.800
That's up to him, isn't it?

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.630
I guess you're still 
just a little girl.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:45.840
Do you know why Sawaki-kun's grandfather

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:47.630
entrusted him to me?

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.890
Well...

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:54.470
Because Sawaki-kun didn't fully 
realize the gravity of his ability,

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:56.770
so he thought you could 
teach him more about it,

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.480
so that he could use 
it more efficiently...

00:13:58.480 --> 00:13:59.900
Yes, thank you.

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:03.900
This is what his grandfather 
said to me...

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:08.090
I want Tadayasu to live his own life.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:11.470
Established in the Muromachi Era 
Sawaki Souemon
Registered Trademark

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:11.510
He wasn't born just to 
take over the business.

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:15.500
He'll be happier if he finds what 
he wants to do himself.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.410
No doubt about it.

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:21.880
That's why he wanted me to give 
him lots of new experiences.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:24.000
Sawaki-kun's father intends

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.430
to make him take over the business,

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:30.040
but his grandfather wants 
to give him more options.

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:33.220
There's no way I could've known that.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:35.750
When he first came here,

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.810
didn't you call him a 
guinea pig? A lab mouse?

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.750
Anyone would think that,

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:42.790
if you told them someone 
who can see microbes

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:44.690
was coming to a place 
that values microbes.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:47.500
Giving him lots of new experiences?

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.820
Letting him find other 
possibilities in Tokyo?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:53.210
Then why do you try 
to keep Sawaki here?

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:56.210
Even if you didn't keep him close 
by like your seminar students,

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.830
couldn't you have still 
watched over him?

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.960
Now, sit down.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:08.090
We don't know yet what Sawaki-kun 
will take an interest in.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:11.220
It could be microbes, or it 
could be something else.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.600
But nurturing comes before discipline.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:16.420
Everything starts after that, right?

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:20.390
I told you, don't be in a hurry.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.850
I-I'm sorry.

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:25.940
He can take his time to decide.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:29.420
If he wants to stay here, 
he should stay as long as he likes.

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:42.420
It will be summer soon.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:06.810
Sawaki?

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:08.530
Y-Yes.

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:22.000
Um...

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:25.330
Hasegawa-san...

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:34.840
Can I keep coming here?

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:38.050
I can't explain why,

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:40.600
but I kind of want to 
learn more about microbes.

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:44.730
I guess... it's because I like them.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.480
Sawaki...

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:12.610
Hey, look at that.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:13.850
What? What?

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:15.300
They're hugging!

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:26.060
Hey, Tadayasu!

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:31.660
Hey...

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:32.790
Yes?

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:35.920
I don't know how to 
make up with people.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.300
What should I do?

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:39.780
I-I don't know either...

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:45.290
By the way, why did you 
lose your ability?

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.840
It happens occasionally.

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:48.790
It does?

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:52.000
I think the last time was 
when I was riding my bike,

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.870
and almost got hit by a car.

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:54.800
A car?

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.690
Yeah. And this time, well...

00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:00.410
there was an unexpected reunion 
and some other stuff...

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:02.310
In short, I guess it happened 
because I was shocked.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:07.430
What the hell?! You wimp!

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:11.150
Self-Sufficiency

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:12.470
Hey, hey!

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:14.170
The shy boy over there!

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:15.930
Are you just going straight home?

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:16.920
Chicken!

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:19.340
If you're a man, 
you should've pushed her down!

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:21.400
Yeah! Just go for it!

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:23.600
Go back there and throw her down!

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:24.660
Throw her down!

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.650
Throw her down!

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.510
Shut up! I only just 
started seeing you again!

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:31.430
You were just ignoring us.

00:18:31.430 --> 00:18:33.170
We've been watching you the whole time!

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.160
We'll brew you good, Tadayasu!

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:37.770
We'll brew you good!

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.930
You guys are such a nuisance.

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:46.410
We'll brew you!

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:55.390
It's finally time to open 
the fermenting cellar.

00:18:55.390 --> 00:18:56.400
Let's celebrate.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:58.360
Fermenting cellar?

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:01.280
I'm going to start making 
liquor in my lab.

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:03.040
That's awesome!

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:05.590
Let's start with beer to 
go along with the season!

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:07.770
This is for research purposes only.

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:10.220
Don't be such a stiff.

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:12.630
Yeah! Let's make sake, too!

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.170
And wine, someday!

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:18.300
Oh, yes. I've contacted Yuuki-kun, too.

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:22.360
I imagine he'll be returning soon.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:24.450
Really?

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:37.520
One, two...

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:41.030
This is the ultimate 
unfiltered nakadori.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.490
I want! Let me have some!

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.160
Chill out, Mutou-san!

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.190
It smells great!

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:27.340
Moyashimon

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:27.340
Episode 11

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:27.340
Microbe Theater 11!

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.340
Microbe Theater

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:33.010
Looks like Tadayasu can see us again.

00:21:33.010 --> 00:21:35.630
Seriously? Should we 
start shouting now?

00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:38.040
It's finally our turn.

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.970
Hold it, everyone!

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:41.340
What is it?

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:43.240
You just said it's our turn,

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:45.630
but this is actually the final episode!

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:47.180
What?!

00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:49.280
What happened with the 
fermenting cellar?

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:52.170
Yeah! The miso, the 
soy sauce, the sake?

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:54.750
Aren't we the stars of Moyashimon?

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:57.120
We haven't even gotten started yet!

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:01.440
We didn't get to brew enough!

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:03.230
Let us brew more!

00:22:03.930 --> 00:22:05.610
Yeah, that's right!

00:22:06.350 --> 00:22:07.140
Huh?

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:12.180
Unfortunately, everyone, this is 
the final episode of Moyashimon...

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:20.210
But we're always close to you!

00:22:20.210 --> 00:22:23.540
We'll coexist with you! 
Don't try to sterilize us!

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:25.890
We'll keep on brewing!

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:28.660
See you next time!
